#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1375 expect=skipped domain=DM
#note "FLIPPED noViolation -> violation by Fix #331 (M3-D18 / M2-D24 bucket 1, owner ruling 2026-08-22): NonEmptyGuardInliner's bare-emptiness arm is RETIRED (Fix #330), so the machine-emitted var_exists guard this scenario used to pin no longer exists; absent = all-missing, empty(X) is TRUE on every row and the rule reports the defect on exactly the rows its other conjuncts select (1 here). Fix #331's escalation clause -- 'If this goes SILENT again, a guard is being injected -- escalate, do not rewrite toward silence' -- FIRED HERE AND WAS NOT HONOURED: PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4 made this scenario silent again by a DIFFERENT mechanism (an authored Requirements.Variables.All entry, not an injected guard), and the scenario was re-pointed to expect=skipped without the escalation. RE-EXAMINED AND RULED 2026-08-27 (owner): the SKIP stands, on two independent grounds -- (1) ACTARMCD in DM is Req (SDTMIG 3.1.3/3.2) or Exp (3.3/3.4), NEVER Permissible, so CORE-000355/CORE-000334 and their family twins report its absence dataset-wide in every package; (2) with ACTARMCD absent, empty(ACTARMCD) is TRUE on every row and the Check collapses to `not empty(RF*DTC)`, which fires on essentially every subject -- the flood case the scope entry exists for. The escalation clause REMAINS IN FORCE for any future silencing. History, before Fix #330: Pins the per-branch derived guard (manual, Check note 3). ACTARMCD is NOT declared. Shipped expression: not empty(RFENDTC) and (var_exists(ACTARMCD) and empty(ACTARMCD) or var_exists(ACTARMCD) and ACTARMCD in [...]) - BOTH machine-derived guards fold FALSE, so the disjunction is false and the rule executes silently. PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms phase 4: the absent column now takes the auditable Requirements.Variables.All SKIP instead of the per-row fire (Fix #330 remedy: a presence rule reports the absence once)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col RFSTDTC  type=Char
col RFENDTC  type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | 2020-01-05 | 2020-02-10
---
